  const trackUrl = 'https://soundcloud.com/artist/track-name';
  let audio;   // will hold the HTML5 Audio object

  SC.resolve(trackUrl).then(track => {
    const streamUrl = `${track.stream_url}?client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID`;
    audio = new Audio(streamUrl);
    audio.controls = false;               // we’ll use our own buttons
    document.getElementById('player-container').appendChild(audio);
  }).catch(err => console.error(err));

  // 3️⃣ Hook up custom UI
  document.getElementById('playBtn').addEventListener('click', () => audio && audio.play());
  document.getElementById('pauseBtn').addEventListener('click', () => audio && audio.pause());

  // 4️⃣ Progress bar
  if (audio) {
    audio.addEventListener('timeupdate', () => {
      const percent = (audio.currentTime / audio.duration) * 100;
      document.getElementById('progress').style.width = percent + '%';
    });
  }
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

*Replace `YOUR_CLIENT_ID` and the `trackUrl` with your own values.*  

---

## 5️⃣ Next Steps & Tips

| Goal | What to do |
|------|------------|
| **Just a single track** | Use the iframe method (no API key). |
| **Custom UI / multiple tracks** | Use the JavaScript SDK as shown above. |
| **User‑specific actions (like uploading, liking)** | Implement OAuth flow with `authenticateUser` (requires client secret). |
| **Responsive design** | Set the iframe width to `100%` and control the max‑width via CSS. |
| **Analytics** | The SDK provides events (`play`, `pause`, `ended`) you can log to your own analytics platform. |
| **Testing** | Use the SoundCloud “Play” button on the track page to verify the stream URL works before embedding. |

---

