## 2. Full OAuth flow – step‑by‑step

### 2.1. Build the **authorization URL** (the link the user clicks)

```text
https://soundcloud.com/connect?
    client_id=client321
    &redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fmywebsite.com%2Fauth%2Fsoundcloud%2Fcallback
    &response_type=code
    &scope=non-expiring
    &state=RANDOM_STRING
```

- **`client_id`** – `client321` (your ID).  
- **`redirect_uri`** – URL‑encoded version of the callback you just registered.  
- **`response_type=code`** – tells SoundCloud to return an authorization **code**.  
- **`scope=non-expiring`** – optional; gives you a long‑lived token (no refresh token needed).  
- **`state`** – a cryptographically random string you generate per request (e.g., `bin2hex(random_bytes(16))`). Store it in the user’s session and verify it on return to protect against CSRF.

Render that URL as a “Log in with SoundCloud” button or link.

