## 7️⃣  Next‑step ideas (optional)

| Idea | Why it’s useful | Quick implementation hint |
|------|----------------|---------------------------|
| **Theme support** (dark mode) | Change `fill` colors of `<text>` and cursor based on a CSS variable. | Use `svg.querySelector('text, rect').style.fill = getComputedStyle(document.body).getPropertyValue('--text-color');` |
| **Progressive reveal** (type‑out a hint before the user focuses) | Gives a “guided‑typing” feel. | Call `animator._setSVGText('Enter your name…')` on page load, then clear on focus. |
| **Accessibility fallback** | Some users disable SVG or have screen readers. | Keep the native `<input>` visible; the SVG is purely decorative (`aria-hidden="true"`). |
| **Export / import settings** | Let power users save their preferred speed. | `exportTypingAnimationSettings({format:'json', svgId:animator.svgId})` → store in `localStorage`. |
| **Multi‑line typing** (for `<textarea>`) | Adjust the SVG viewBox height dynamically based on line‑count. | After each `_setSVGText`, compute `lines = str.split('\n').length; svg.setAttribute('height', 30*lines);` |

